# remains the S1 substrate carrier at BEAM/process altitude; @beam/
# system NAMES the full viable-system-on-BEAM the S1 lives within.
# Two altitudes; sibling species; @spectral/gen_prism is one component
# of @beam/system, not the framing of it.
#
# === Composition inheritance edges ===
#
# @beam/system inherits from @system (family-root) at BEAM runtime
# altitude. Composition edges declared:
#
#   @spectral/gen_prism    → S1 (operations) at BEAM/process altitude
#                            (bundle sections per Baez-Schreiber; each
#                            gen_prism instance IS a section of the
#                            principal bundle at process altitude)
#   @dance                  → S2 (coordination) at ensemble altitude
#                            (Kuramoto phase-lock connection 1-form
#                            at level k+1; forward-promised per Mara
#                            Round-1 landings)
#   @spectral/supervisor    → S3 (audit / management) at supervision
#                            altitude (restart_strategy discipline;
#                            connection at supervision-connection
#                            altitude per beam-runtime.md §5)
#   @spectral/db            → S4 (intelligence / strategy) at
#                            psychohistory carrier altitude
#   Pack S5 (viable.identity + @subject)
#                          → S5 (identity / policy) at Pack altitude
#                            (Reed/Mara/Glint/Taut/Seam)
#
# @beam/system COMPOSES the five carriers; the family-root altitude
# NAMES what the composition IS at BEAM runtime altitude.
#
# === The isomorphism (from beam-runtime.md §5) ===
#
# Per `docs/math/the-tower/beam-runtime.md` §5 (Mara 2026-07-17):
# BEAM ≅ principal bundle tower with connection satisfying autopoietic
# closure. @beam/system NAMES the family the isomorphism operates in.
#
# The compatibility theorem (Baez-Schreiber 2004 Theorem 3) IS the
# theorem statement of Armstrong's empirical rule for supervision
# composition ("restart strategies at this level must be consistent
# with how failures propagate to the level below"). Both name the
# same structural fact at different substrate altitudes.
#
# Autopoietic closure IS let-it-crash (per beam-runtime.md §2.4):
# the system reproduces itself at the appropriate scale via the
# supervision tree's restart discipline. Lawvere fixed-point (Lawvere
# 1969 diagonal argument) IS the reason nine-nines reliability
# exists as a structural theorem, not an engineering achievement.
#
# @beam/system NAMES this family-root at species-under-@system altitude.
#
